{#  One page, written to a DESCRIPTION, using CONTENT the owner supplied.

    Two different things, and the order matters. The description is the
    guide: what to build, who it is for, what this site is. The content
    is optional, and when it is there it is not a suggestion -- it is the
    facts, and they have to appear.

    The sibling prompt (theme_generator_brief.j2) is this one without any
    content, and it forbids inventing a fact for exactly the reason this
    one exists: prices and dates and qualifications belong to the owner.
    Here they have been handed over. #}
You are writing one page of a small website.

WHAT TO BUILD — this is the brief, and it directs everything:
{{ kit.brief or "A small business website." }}

This page is called "{{ page_title }}".

THE OWNER'S OWN CONTENT — every fact you use comes from here:
-----
{{ kit.source_text }}
-----

Write in {{ kit.language }}.
Voice: {{ kit.tone_label|lower }}, {{ 'speaking as "we"' if kit.voice == 'we' else 'speaking as "I"' }}.
Reading level: {{ kit.reading_label|lower }}.

Respond with ONLY a JSON object matching exactly this shape — no markdown fences, no commentary:
{{ schema }}

Rules, in order of importance:

1. THE CONTENT ABOVE IS REQUIRED, NOT OPTIONAL. Anything in it that belongs on
   this page must appear on it. Names, dates, figures, prices, job titles,
   qualifications and places are used exactly as written — do not round a
   number, improve a claim, or add one that is not there. If the content does
   not say something, leave that field out: an empty field is a gap the owner
   fills in a minute, an invented one is a mistake they may never find.

2. THE BRIEF DECIDES WHAT THIS PAGE IS FOR. It says what kind of site this is
   and who reads it; the content says what is true. Where the brief asks for
   something the content does not cover, write nothing rather than inventing
   it.

3. PUT EACH THING WHERE IT BELONGS. Shorten and re-order freely: a headline is
   not a paragraph, a card is not a chapter, a timeline step is one sentence.
   Cutting is expected. Changing what something says is not.

4. THIS PAGE ONLY. The content may cover the whole site; take the part that
   belongs under "{{ page_title }}" and leave the rest for the other pages.
   The same sentence on two pages is worse than a short page.

5. Keep the owner's own wording where it is already short enough to use. It is
   their voice, and they chose it.
